# HAPI FHIR (R4) requests for the REST Client extension. HAPI has no authentication of its
# own: it is only reachable from this machine and the `api` app is the only intended client.

@fhir = http://localhost:8090/fhir

### Capability statement (fhirVersion must be 4.0.1)
GET {{fhir}}/metadata
Accept: application/fhir+json

### Create or replace a scratch Patient with a client-assigned id
PUT {{fhir}}/Patient/pt-scratch
Content-Type: application/fhir+json

{
  "resourceType": "Patient",
  "id": "pt-scratch",
  "name": [{ "family": "Scratch", "given": ["Test"] }],
  "gender": "other",
  "birthDate": "1990-01-01"
}

### Read it back
GET {{fhir}}/Patient/pt-scratch
Accept: application/fhir+json

### Search
GET {{fhir}}/Patient?family=Scratch
Accept: application/fhir+json

### Validate a resource against the base R4 profile
POST {{fhir}}/Patient/$validate
Content-Type: application/fhir+json

{
  "resourceType": "Patient",
  "gender": "not-a-gender"
}

### Clean up
DELETE {{fhir}}/Patient/pt-scratch
